    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened in 1909, and Rondo was formally incorporated on June 19, 1918, adding a depot, churches, and a school.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/rondo_arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1908, Rondo already hosted a Nehi soda plant, a sawmill, and a hand‑operated water pump, serving a cotton and timber economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23,
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/rondo_arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Today, Rondo has no commercial businesses left, with only Rondo Baptist Church still active and a modest city hall for residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/rondo_arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Rondo sits at 34°39′33″N, 90°49′14″W, 213 feet above sea level, covering just over one square mile.",
